 "protocol": "Domain check: rows are the synthetic benign sandbox txs (label 1, group = sandbox family) and real normals from the train and calibration months only (label 0, group = month), the real ones sampled per flow type to the synthetic flow mix with one common ratio (at most 3 real per synthetic, seed 0). Classifier: HistGradientBoostingClassifier (seed 0) on tx_features, out-of-fold ROC-AUC with 5-fold StratifiedGroupKFold. Pass: AUC <= 0.75. Otherwise drop, one at a time, the kept feature with the largest univariate |AUC - 0.5| on the same rows and re-run, for at most floor(0.5 * n_features) drops; if the AUC is still above 0.75 the head is not used. Head (only after a pass, on the kept features): the same classifier with balanced class weights, positives = all synthetic attack txs (exploit and attempt), negatives = synthetic benign plus real train-month normals. Head thresholds on calibration normals with md.alert_threshold, intents_v1's combined alerts using the budget first, so the combined calibration alert rate stays at most 1/10,000 (high) and 1/1,000 (medium). Combined label = max(intents_v1 label, head label). Adopt iff, on real held-out campaign txs with role exploit or attempt, medium-or-above detections rise by at least 5, AND on sealed test normals the head adds at most floor(n_test / 1,000) medium-or-above and at most floor(n_test / 10,000) high alerts. Thresholds are never tuned on the test slice or on real campaigns.",
